{"file_type": "RF_VCB_PROJECT", "file_version": 2, "title": "", "creation_date": 1749068803, "last_edit_date": 1794784381, "time_worked_on": 190471, "layers": ["", "", ""], "assembly": "# Advent of Code 2025, day 2 part 2 (Gift Shop)\n#\n# The answer is the sum of every ID in the input ranges that is some digits repeated at least twice\n# (12341234, 123123123, 1111111). An ID of n digits made of a block of k digits is h * M, where\n# M = (10^n - 1) / (10^k - 1), for example 1001001 for n = 9, k = 3. A family is one pair (n, k). For\n# each range and each family the program walks to the first such number that is not below the range's\n# first ID and adds up the ones in the range.\n#\n# Some IDs are in two families: 222222 is 222 twice and 22 three times. So for 6 and for 10 digits the\n# family of the single repeated digit (k = 1) is subtracted once. Those sums go to NEG, and at the end\n# SUM = SUM - NEG.\n#\n# Result, when the CPU stops on the Breakpoint at END:\n#   0x0100-0x0102  the sum as three 16-bit words, low word first\n#   0x0110-0x011E  the sum as 15 decimal digits, one per word, most significant first\n#   (0x0104-0x0106 holds NEG, the part that was subtracted)\n#\n# Input (rule 1 of RULES.md): each range is its first and last ID, each ID three 16-bit words, low word\n# first; three zero words end the list. Built-in limits: IDs of at most 10 digits, a sum\n# below 2^48.\n#\n# A number is three words (16 bits each). The CPU's registers are 32 bits wide, so a word is added in a\n# register and the carry is what ends up in the register's upper half (rgAH).\n# The CPU has no multiply, divide or shift; see findings/cpu-instructions.md.\n\nsymbol nop 0b0000_0000_0000_0000\nsymbol ld  0b0010_0000_0000_0000\nsymbol lia 0b0011_0000_0000_0000\nsymbol lib 0b0100_0000_0000_0000\nsymbol sto 0b0101_0000_0000_0000\n\nmacro  load  { ld  | a? | (b? >> 6) }\nmacro  store { sto | a? | (b? >> 6) }\n\nsymbol sum    0b0110_0100_0000_0000\nsymbol sum_32 0b0110_1100_0000_0000\nsymbol sub    0b0110_0010_0000_0000\nsymbol sub_32 0b0110_1010_0000_0000\nsymbol shf    0b0110_0001_0000_0000\nsymbol shf_32 0b0110_1001_0000_0000\nsymbol and    0b0110_0000_1000_0000\nsymbol and_32 0b0110_1000_1000_0000\nsymbol or     0b0110_0000_0100_0000\nsymbol or_32  0b0110_1000_0100_0000\nsymbol xor    0b0110_0000_0010_0000\nsymbol xor_32 0b0110_1000_0010_0000\nsymbol neg    0b0110_0000_0001_0000\nsymbol neg_32 0b0110_1000_0001_0000\n\nsymbol psh 0b1010_0000_0000_0000\nsymbol pop 0b1011_0000_0000_0000\n\nsymbol jmp  0b1100_0000_0000_0000\nsymbol call 0b1110_0000_0000_0000\nsymbol ret  0b1111_0000_0000_0000\n\nsymbol rgAH 0b1000_0000_0000\nsymbol rgA  0b0100_0000_0000\nsymbol rgBH 0b0010_0000_0000\nsymbol rgB  0b0001_0000_0000\nsymbol rgSP 0b0000_1000_0000\nsymbol rgSB 0b0000_0100_0000\nsymbol non  0\n\nsymbol zero  0b1000_0000_0000 \nsymbol carry 0b0100_0000_0000\nsymbol nega  0b0010_0000_0000\nsymbol eq    0b0001_0000_0000\nsymbol neq   0b0000_1000_0000\n\n# ---- Variables (all below 0x1000, so lia/lib can address them) ----\n# The result\npointer SUM_0 0x0100 0\npointer SUM_1 0x0101 0\npointer SUM_2 0x0102 0\n# What must be subtracted from SUM at the end\npointer NEG_0 0x0104 0\npointer NEG_1 0x0105 0\npointer NEG_2 0x0106 0\n# The current range: its first and last ID. HI must follow LO.\npointer LO_0 0x0120 0\npointer LO_1 0x0121 0\npointer LO_2 0x0122 0\npointer HI_0 0x0123 0\npointer HI_1 0x0124 0\npointer HI_2 0x0125 0\n# The current family: NEXT is where the next family starts in the table, SIGN is 1 when its IDs are\n# subtracted, C the candidate ID, LAST the family's largest candidate. SIGN, C and LAST must follow NEXT.\npointer NEXT 0x0130 0\npointer SIGN 0x0131 0\npointer C_0 0x0132 0\npointer C_1 0x0133 0\npointer C_2 0x0134 0\npointer LAST_0 0x0135 0\npointer LAST_1 0x0136 0\npointer LAST_2 0x0137 0\n# S is the current step, T a trial value, COUNT how often STEP_UP stepped\npointer S_0 0x0140 0\npointer S_1 0x0141 0\npointer S_2 0x0142 0\npointer T_0 0x0143 0\npointer T_1 0x0144 0\npointer T_2 0x0145 0\npointer COUNT 0x0146 0\n# The constant 1 as a number\npointer ONE_0 0x0150 1\npointer ONE_1 0x0151 0\npointer ONE_2 0x0152 0\n# Pointers: SRC and DST for COPY_1, IN the next input word, DIGIT the next digit to write,\n# and the addresses of the two tables\npointer SRC 0x0160 0\npointer DST 0x0161 0\npointer IN 0x0162 0x2000\npointer DIGIT 0x0163 0x0110\npointer K_TABLE 0x0164 0x3000\npointer POWERS 0x0165 0x3100\n\n# ---- The CPU starts at 0xFF00 ----\norigin 0xFF00\njmp; MAIN\n\norigin 0x1000\n@ MAIN\n# Read the next range into LO and HI\n@ NEXT_RANGE\n\tlia IN; load rgA rgA; lib SRC; store rgA rgB\n\tlia LO_0; lib DST; store rgA rgB\n\tcall; COPY_3\n\tcall; COPY_3\n\tlia SRC; load rgA rgA; lib IN; store rgA rgB\n\t# A first ID of 0 ends the list\n\tlia LO_0; load rgA rgA; lib LO_1; load rgB rgB; or; lib LO_2; load rgB rgB; or; lib 0\n\tjmp eq; ALL_RANGES_DONE\n\tlia K_TABLE; load rgA rgA; lib SRC; store rgA rgB\n\n# Read the next family from the table: NEXT, SIGN, C = its smallest candidate, LAST = its largest\n@ NEXT_K\n\tlia NEXT; lib DST; store rgA rgB\n\tcall; COPY_1\n\tcall; COPY_1\n\tcall; COPY_3\n\tcall; COPY_3\n\tlia NEXT; load rgA rgA; lib 0\n\tjmp eq; NEXT_RANGE\n\t# No candidate of this family is in the range when even the largest is below LO\n\t# compare LAST with LO: nega if LAST < LO, zero if equal\n\tlia LAST_2; load rgA rgA; lib LO_2; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_1\n\tlia LAST_1; load rgA rgA; lib LO_1; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_1\n\tlia LAST_0; load rgA rgA; lib LO_0; load rgB rgB\n@ CMP_1\n\tsub\n\tjmp nega; SKIP_K\n\n# Walk C up to the largest candidate below LO, in steps of M * 10^j, largest step first.\n# The steps are the rest of this family's table entry.\n@ NEXT_STEP\n\tlia SRC; load rgA rgA; lib NEXT; load rgB rgB\n\tjmp eq; STEPS_DONE\n\tlia S_0; lib DST; store rgA rgB\n\tcall; COPY_3\n\tcall; STEP_UP\n\tjmp; NEXT_STEP\n\n# S is now M. If C is still below LO, the next candidate is the first one in the range.\n@ STEPS_DONE\n\t# compare C with LO: nega if C < LO, zero if equal\n\tlia C_2; load rgA rgA; lib LO_2; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_2\n\tlia C_1; load rgA rgA; lib LO_1; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_2\n\tlia C_0; load rgA rgA; lib LO_0; load rgB rgB\n@ CMP_2\n\tsub\n\tjmp nega; ONE_MORE\n\tjmp; ADD_CANDIDATES\n@ ONE_MORE\n\t# C = C + S\n\tlia C_0; load rgA rgA; lib S_0; load rgB rgB; sum; lib C_0; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia C_1; load rgA rgA; sum; lib S_1; load rgB rgB; sum; lib C_1; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia C_2; load rgA rgA; sum; lib S_2; load rgB rgB; sum; lib C_2; store rgA rgB\n\n# Add every candidate up to HI (and up to LAST) to SUM, or to NEG when SIGN is 1\n@ ADD_CANDIDATES\n\t# compare HI with C: nega if HI < C, zero if equal\n\tlia HI_2; load rgA rgA; lib C_2; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_3\n\tlia HI_1; load rgA rgA; lib C_1; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_3\n\tlia HI_0; load rgA rgA; lib C_0; load rgB rgB\n@ CMP_3\n\tsub\n\tjmp nega; NEXT_K\n\t# compare LAST with C: nega if LAST < C, zero if equal\n\tlia LAST_2; load rgA rgA; lib C_2; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_4\n\tlia LAST_1; load rgA rgA; lib C_1; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_4\n\tlia LAST_0; load rgA rgA; lib C_0; load rgB rgB\n@ CMP_4\n\tsub\n\tjmp nega; NEXT_K\n\tlia SIGN; load rgA rgA; lib 0\n\tjmp eq; ADD_TO_SUM\n\t# NEG = NEG + C\n\tlia NEG_0; load rgA rgA; lib C_0; load rgB rgB; sum; lib NEG_0; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia NEG_1; load rgA rgA; sum; lib C_1; load rgB rgB; sum; lib NEG_1; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia NEG_2; load rgA rgA; sum; lib C_2; load rgB rgB; sum; lib NEG_2; store rgA rgB\n\tjmp; STEP_ON\n@ ADD_TO_SUM\n\t# SUM = SUM + C\n\tlia SUM_0; load rgA rgA; lib C_0; load rgB rgB; sum; lib SUM_0; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia SUM_1; load rgA rgA; sum; lib C_1; load rgB rgB; sum; lib SUM_1; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia SUM_2; load rgA rgA; sum; lib C_2; load rgB rgB; sum; lib SUM_2; store rgA rgB\n@ STEP_ON\n\t# C = C + S\n\tlia C_0; load rgA rgA; lib S_0; load rgB rgB; sum; lib C_0; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia C_1; load rgA rgA; sum; lib S_1; load rgB rgB; sum; lib C_1; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia C_2; load rgA rgA; sum; lib S_2; load rgB rgB; sum; lib C_2; store rgA rgB\n\tjmp; ADD_CANDIDATES\n\n@ SKIP_K\n\tlia NEXT; load rgA rgA; lib SRC; store rgA rgB\n\tjmp; NEXT_K\n\n# Take off what was counted twice. Then write the sum as decimal digits: count how often each power\n# of ten fits, largest power first. This is the same walk as above, from C = 0 towards LO = SUM + 1.\n@ ALL_RANGES_DONE\n\t# SUM = SUM - NEG. A word's borrow shows as 0xFFFF in rgAH; copied into both halves of B it is -1.\n\tlia SUM_0; load rgA rgA; lib NEG_0; load rgB rgB; sub; lib SUM_0; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; psh rgAH; pop rgBH; lia SUM_1; load rgA rgA; sum; lib NEG_1; load rgB rgB; sub; lib SUM_1; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; psh rgAH; pop rgBH; lia SUM_2; load rgA rgA; sum; lib NEG_2; load rgB rgB; sub; lib SUM_2; store rgA rgB\n\t# LO = SUM + ONE\n\tlia SUM_0; load rgA rgA; lib ONE_0; load rgB rgB; sum; lib LO_0; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia SUM_1; load rgA rgA; sum; lib ONE_1; load rgB rgB; sum; lib LO_1; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia SUM_2; load rgA rgA; sum; lib ONE_2; load rgB rgB; sum; lib LO_2; store rgA rgB\n\tlia 0; lib C_0; store rgA rgB; lib C_1; store rgA rgB; lib C_2; store rgA rgB\n\tlia POWERS; load rgA rgA; lib SRC; store rgA rgB\n@ NEXT_DIGIT\n\tlia S_0; lib DST; store rgA rgB\n\tcall; COPY_3\n\t# A power of 0 ends the table\n\tlia S_0; load rgA rgA; lib S_1; load rgB rgB; or; lib S_2; load rgB rgB; or; lib 0\n\tjmp eq; END\n\tcall; STEP_UP\n\tlia COUNT; load rgA rgA; lib DIGIT; load rgB rgB; store rgA rgB\n\tlia DIGIT; load rgA rgA; lib 1; sum; lib DIGIT; store rgA rgB\n\tjmp; NEXT_DIGIT\n\n@ END\n\tnon\n\n# ---- Subroutines ----\norigin 0x1800\n# STEP_UP: add S to C as often as the result stays below LO. COUNT is the number of steps.\n@ STEP_UP\n\tlia 0; lib COUNT; store rgA rgB\n@ STEP_UP_AGAIN\n\t# T = C + S\n\tlia C_0; load rgA rgA; lib S_0; load rgB rgB; sum; lib T_0; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia C_1; load rgA rgA; sum; lib S_1; load rgB rgB; sum; lib T_1; store rgA rgB\n\tpsh rgAH; pop rgB; lia C_2; load rgA rgA; sum; lib S_2; load rgB rgB; sum; lib T_2; store rgA rgB\n\t# compare T with LO: nega if T < LO, zero if equal\n\tlia T_2; load rgA rgA; lib LO_2; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_5\n\tlia T_1; load rgA rgA; lib LO_1; load rgB rgB; jmp neq; CMP_5\n\tlia T_0; load rgA rgA; lib LO_0; load rgB rgB\n@ CMP_5\n\tsub\n\tjmp nega; STEP_UP_TAKE\n\tret\n@ STEP_UP_TAKE\n\tlia T_0; load rgA rgA; lib C_0; store rgA rgB; lia T_1; load rgA rgA; lib C_1; store rgA rgB; lia T_2; load rgA rgA; lib C_2; store rgA rgB\n\tlia COUNT; load rgA rgA; lib 1; sum; lib COUNT; store rgA rgB\n\tjmp; STEP_UP_AGAIN\n\n# COPY_3: copy three words from the address in SRC to the address in DST; both move on by three.\n@ COPY_3\n\tcall; COPY_1\n\tcall; COPY_1\n\tcall; COPY_1\n\tret\n\n# COPY_1: copy one word from the address in SRC to the address in DST; both move on by one.\n@ COPY_1\n\tlib SRC; load rgB rgB; load rgA rgB; lib DST; load rgB rgB; store rgA rgB\n\tlia SRC; load rgA rgA; lib 1; sum; lib SRC; store rgA rgB\n\tlia DST; load rgA rgA; lib 1; sum; lib DST; store rgA rgB\n\tret\n\n# ---- The table of families ----\n# Per family: the address of the next entry; SIGN; the smallest candidate 10^(k-1) * M; the largest,\n# 10^n - 1; then the steps M * 10^j for j = k-1 down to 0. An entry with address 0 ends it.\norigin 0x3000\n# 2 digits, a block of 1 repeated 2 times: M = 11, candidates 11 to 99\n0x300B; 0\n0x000B; 0x0000; 0x0000\n0x0063; 0x0000; 0x0000\n0x000B; 0x0000; 0x0000\n# 3 digits, a block of 1 repeated 3 times: M = 111, candidates 111 to 999\n0x3016; 0\n0x006F; 0x0000; 0x0000\n0x03E7; 0x0000; 0x0000\n0x006F; 0x0000; 0x0000\n# 4 digits, a block of 2 repeated 2 times: M = 101